WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.120
Associate Professor Casimir Beng leads the Adaptive Metrics Lab at Slop University.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.500
I trained as a control engineer.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.910
Now I study the measures that organisations run on.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.010
The beep at the self-checkout.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.190
The tick box that says a worker was tested.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.190
The smart sprinkler on the quad.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.700
Each one says it measures something.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.486
My lab checks whether it does.

00:00:24.286 --> 00:00:28.476
That work has made him the University's most published and most cited researcher.

00:00:29.076 --> 00:00:31.056
Three hundred and eleven research outputs.

00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:33.436
Fifteen hundred and sixty-one citations.

00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:36.436
And an h-index of thirty-two.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:38.766
I still think like an engineer.

00:00:39.066 --> 00:00:40.816
If the gauge says the tank is full,

00:00:41.016 --> 00:00:42.936
someone should go and look in the tank.

00:00:43.536 --> 00:00:44.486
Visit the website,

00:00:44.686 --> 00:00:45.926
follow us on Bluesky,

00:00:46.126 --> 00:00:47.146
or send us an email.
